The problem is to allocate different types of boats (from products.csv) to different display areas (from capacity.csv) to maximize total value, subject to each area's capacity. The decision variables $x_{ij}$ represent the number of units of boat type $j$ in display area $i$, and must be nonnegative integers. Each boat type has a value and a weight (size). Each display area has a capacity. The objective is to maximize total value. For each display area $i$, the sum of the weights of all boats assigned to it cannot exceed its capacity.

Let:
- $i$ index display areas (DisplayID from capacity.csv, 1 to 14)
- $j$ index boat types (ProductName from products.csv, 1 to 20)
- $c_i$ = Capacity of display area $i$
- $v_j$ = Value of boat type $j$
- $w_j$ = Weight of boat type $j$
- $x_{ij}$ = number of units of boat type $j$ in display area $i$ (integer, $\geq 0$)

